#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Render author B's frozen conditional reading and complete native-position audit."""
import json,pathlib
BASE=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
a=json.loads((BASE/'artifacts/B_ACCOUNT.json').read_text())
def esc(x):return str(x).replace('|','&#124;').replace('\n',' ')
def short(v):
 if isinstance(v,dict):
  keys=['type','id','kind','predicate','wind_id','source','phase','new_wind','previous_wind','preceding_wind','old_wind','horizon','status','selected_wind','episode']
  return ','.join(k+'='+str(v[k]) for k in keys if k in v)
 return str(v)
text='''# Author B: solar succession after cessation

This is a partial strict whole account, with an operationally connected IT reading of N19 and E27. N has no retained contribution gap; E has three explicitly unused reference outputs. No constructor or exact assignment was changed to remove them. All English meanings are C0 hypotheses. The clauses below describe physical winds and their generation and cessation within one generic conditional; they do not assert that an observed storm occurred or that the manuscript supplies a confirmed wind lexeme.

## Connected reading

Suppose a wind of kind K is blowing from source P within the observer's horizon H while the Sun is at that source and dry material M is available. P and Q are adjacent sources in this same horizon. Turn attention to Q, where this case has not yet registered a wind, and then return to P and bind the wind there to its present state. As the Sun withdraws from P, that wind ceases. Subsequently the Sun approaches adjacent Q and raises dry material there; from this raised material a fresh wind is generated. Bind that new wind to its solar material origin and its current state. Its generation follows the preceding wind's cessation, and its source is adjacent to the preceding source. Recall the preceding wind and its solar withdrawal cause, then turn to the new source and bind the wind now blowing there. Bind that latest generated wind again: it is a different physical wind from the preceding one, has the solar material origin just described, and comes from the adjacent source. Thus this wind is the solar successor of the wind that ceased.

Continue with that same newly generated wind as the preceding wind for the next succession, retaining its identity, source, horizon and ordered time. Recall it and its written state: as the Sun withdraws from its source Q it ceases. Attention turns toward P. Subsequently the Sun approaches P and raises dry material there. A fresh wind is generated from this material, with a fresh identity distinct both from the just-ended wind at Q and from the original ended wind at P. Bind this new wind and its solar material origin. Its source P is adjacent to Q and its identity differs from the just-ended wind. Bind the latest generated wind again: its generation follows the preceding cessation; the preceding wind ceased because of solar withdrawal; the new wind is blowing, comes from the adjacent source and has the solar material origin. Recall this latest wind and its fresh generation: its identity is distinct and its generation is later than the preceding cessation. Recall the preceding wind, reaffirm that it ceased, and return attention to the latest generated wind. Thus this wind is the solar successor of the preceding wind. Bind the latest wind's current state once more, and certify that the previous wind's solar withdrawal and cessation preceded this generation before binding the latest wind again and reaffirming the succession.

The first paragraph covers every IT N whole in source order, .2–.6; the second covers every IT E whole in source order, .7–.11. The repeated recalls and bindings are retained because their whole forms are present. They do not justify claiming that every returned reference is useful: the attention turn at E .7, the previous-wind recall at E .10 and the first final binding at E .11 have no actual later reference consumer under the frozen rules. The connected paragraph preserves them as authored clauses while the strict account remains partial.

## Physical referents and actual ordering

The original conditional participant is u at P, initially blowing at phase 0. N explicitly causes its cessation at phase 1, raises material at Q at phase 2 and generates v1 at Q at phase 3. E's written pchedeey bridge consumes the N anchor and promotes this same v1 to preceding participant without resetting world, time or observer. E causes v1's cessation at phase 4, raises material at P at phase 5 and generates v2 at P at phase 6. The final state has u and v1 ceased and v2 blowing. Returning to P does not revive u. The phase numbers encode order only; no measured delay, sunrise clock, cardinal direction or required empty interval is supplied.

WITHDRAW, APPROACH and GENERATE clauses actually update the conditional physical world when executed. They are not stored unexecuted instructions. Withdrawal causes the corresponding cessation, solar approach causes material raising, and generation consumes that raised material and its approach provenance. The comparison and final succession predicates consume written wind anchors, generation and cessation events, source adjacency and causal provenance. Replacing the new wind by continued same-ID blowing of the old wind falsifies the distinctness and cessation-before-generation predicates. Changing Q to the same or a nonadjacent source falsifies adjacency. Removing solar material provenance falsifies the claimed cause. These are consequences of the authored meanings, not independently observed manuscript discriminators. A static description of two time-indexed states with these same physical IDs, activity, generation, cause and adjacency would express equivalent content.

## Shared aN effect

Bare aiin is the root aN, not a child of d or any other head. It constructs an explicit WindAnchor of the selected physical ID, source, horizon, ordered reference phase, current wind activity and generation/cessation provenance. There is no automatic conversion from a selected wind to such an anchor. The N bare aiin anchor is consumed by withdrawal; shodaiin uses fixed So·daN (So=[S,o], daN=[d,[a,N]]) to certify solar material origin, select the latest generated physical wind and execute the same aN operation; its anchor is consumed by ordered-time and adjacency comparisons. N and E daiin select the latest actually generated wind and execute that same root, with later physical consumers. This satisfies the authored non-null shared interface on all three licensed forms while leaving meaning unconfirmed. shedaiin is separately priced Se·daN, and oraiin performs the same source-next operation followed by aN. The unparsed whole oteey supplies an origin assertion and an explicit anchor through a paid exact sequence, without claiming an aiin spelling or new productive parser.

## Costs, retained limits and reader sensitivity

The immutable initial freeze has 12 constructor families, eight opaque constants, 13 exact whole assignments, eight ambient reference registers and three source-next policies (unique participant selects; no participant preserves identity without a matching-source claim; multiple participants block). Six starting premises supply observer-relative H, adjacent P/Q, potential original wind u of kind K, initial Sun/material availability, generic conditional scope and phase/cursor initialization. Extensions add 37 separately paid exact assignments, 12 semantic type schemas, explicit solar-event expansions, one N-to-E episode bridge and the non-aiin anchor alias. There are 50 assigned exact form types and 112 unassigned raw types. Aliases are individually priced; no raw variants are automatically equated. Fresh v1/v2 are generated physical instance IDs, not additional opaque lexical names. The initial conditional supplies substantial semantic content: these costs are not inferred translations or evidence for the candidate.

The lexical sain setup explicitly opens this hypothetical case after the unaccounted outside prefix. Nothing makes .1 inert or completes it. No line or paragraph boundary resets the model. Unknown words taint continuity, so assigned entries after them retain their exact rule but do not execute on an assumed preserved world. Unknown carry assumptions, instruction defaults, semantic-null rules and new parser families are all zero. S, W and .24 therefore remain partial, not accidental repetitions validated by a continuation. All assigned repeats, including or, shedy, daiin, bare aiin and tedy, retain the identical entry in all 473 native positions.

There are five ZL execution-dependent uncertain small-gap boundaries, individually paid in the account: N .2 or + aiin, .3 olfar + ary, .4 chol + daiin; E .10 ytchedy + qodar and .11 soiis + aiin. The ZL reading provisionally treats these as separate lexical boundaries; a joint hardchunk analysis is unresolved. Raw native separators and groups are unchanged. Nine further small-gap seams outside the executed primary reading remain uncertain without an execution assumption. No ZL completeness claim is unconditional on segmentation.

IT N is operationally 19/19 and contribution-complete within its paid conditional premises. IT E is operationally 27/27 but strict partial: fcheey's temporary source focus is overwritten without being consumed, qokar's old-wind reference is overwritten while qotchd independently reads the old register, and bare aiin's final anchor is overwritten by shedaiin's anchor. These three gaps remain visible. ZL N reaches 19/19 conditional on its three native boundary assumptions. ZL E reaches 26/27, has the analogous three gaps plus an unconsumed final shedaiin anchor, and stops at literal chok{co}m, which is unknown rather than IT chokcod. RF N reaches 16/19 and stops at literal ol@176;ar; the subsequent N and all E clauses are blocked by this unknown continuity, so RF E is 0/27. RF entities and marked raw forms are not silently substituted.

The mandatory .13 or shedy tedy sequence is preserved with its native neighbours. Unknown .12 words prevent an assumed carry of N/E physical bindings into it. or and shedy keep their declared B meanings, and tedy keeps its declared ordered-generation comparison, but they are blocked rather than claimed as a successful conversion. sodaiiin and chy remain unknown. Literal RF {ch'}edy remains distinct from shedy. IDEA582's original Assertable/DescriptionRef type clash is unchanged; this different hypothetical interface does not rescue that failure.

ZL, IT and RF are alternate readings of one f85 leaf. Their repeats are not three independent confirmations. No new images, reserve data, corpus queries, historical efficacy claims or competing author content were used. Technical replay and source conservation do not establish a semantic winner, a relation score, a wind-name interpretation or a predecessor reopening.

## Native-position coverage and barriers

The following summaries and complete 473-row audit are generated from B_ACCOUNT.json. The JSON retains all 12 native fields, every typed argument's actual value and producer, returned typed values, state/delta, later consumers, exact dictionary entry, seam assumptions and row costs. ACCOUNTED_C0 means execution within the declared generic case, not confirmed translation. UNKNOWN is unassigned and non-inert. BLOCKED_MISSING_INITIAL_INPUTS has no written initial case. BLOCKED_UNPROVEN_UNKNOWN_BRIDGE has a retained rule but no licensed continuity. The three IT contribution gaps remain ACCOUNTED_C0 operational rows with explicit unused-reference flags; they prevent a strict whole-account PASS.

'''
text+='| Reader | Unit | Executed/native | Strict complete | Native boundary assumptions | First strict barrier |\n|---|---|---:|---|---:|---|\n'
for u in a['primary_units']:
 b=u['first_barrier'];text+='| '+esc(u['reader'])+' | '+u['block']+' | '+str(u['accounted_count'])+'/'+str(u['count'])+' | '+str(u['complete'])+' | '+str(len(u['boundary_assumption_ids']))+' | '+esc(b['source_group_id']+' '+b['raw'] if b else 'none')+' |\n'
text+='\n| Reader | Operational status | Rows |\n|---|---|---:|\n'
for x in a['literal_coverage_by_reader_status']:text+='| '+x['reader']+' | '+x['status']+' | '+str(x['rows'])+' |\n'
text+='\n## Complete ordered native-row audit\n\nArguments below identify actual typed operands; full values and producer links remain in JSON. A blank output means no execution rather than an inert lexical value. Costs refer to the fixed exact dictionary entry, with additional boundary assumptions shown where used.\n\n| Native ID | Raw group | Rule / price | Status | Actual arguments | Returned values | Later consumers / unused gap |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n'
for r in a['rows']:
 rule=(r['entry_id'] or 'UNKNOWN')+' / '+r['cost']['kind']
 if r.get('boundary_assumption_ids'):rule+=' / '+','.join(r['boundary_assumption_ids'])
 args='; '.join(x['role']+':'+short(x['value']) for x in r['arguments'])
 outs='; '.join(short(v) for v in r['returns'])
 consumption=', '.join(r['consumer_source_ids']) or r.get('contribution_status') or r.get('terminal_contribution') or r.get('reason','')
 text+='| '+' | '.join(esc(x) for x in [r['source_group_id'],r['ivtff_group_raw'],rule,r['status'],args,outs,consumption])+' |\n'
text+='\nAll source-native IDs, paragraph marks, positions, group counts, raw entities and left/right separators remain unchanged in B_ACCOUNT.json. No author A/C or critic content was read before this freeze.\n'
(BASE/'artifacts/B_READING.md').write_text(text)
